      "writtenOn": "2024-05-23T19:41:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we did agree that, currently, there\u0027s nothing specifically preventing a profile from starting before its parent. However:\n* that\u0027s certainly not a normal situation, and I doubt it could happen in real life except through this mechanism\n* one day it might get prevented\n* I was speaking about *starting* the profile. Here we\u0027re presumably talking about *unlocking* the profile. Again, it probably isn\u0027t *prevented* from a Multiuser perspective, but mostly because, except for RoR, it was probably impossible anyway.\n\nI do think the idea of unlocking a profile even if we fail to unlock its parent is a dangerous one. Even if it doesn\u0027t cause issues now, it might one day, since it\u0027s definitely not an expected scenario.",
      "parentUuid": "6d338c08_4bdadea7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 472,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 473,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "c5a6f325f5d92956cdba086f23f078afc220fc69",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
